clean_summary:
Improve your agents with one weird trick: ECHO suggests that when you fine-tune an agent, you should not only train it to predict the agent's replies but also the terminal responses. When using GRPO, you can leverage the same rollout to predict terminal responses with cross-entropy loss. This approach provides additional supervision from the command line interface (CLI) at no extra cost.

This method apparently helps the model develop a 'world model' of the terminal, leading to improved performance, which was surprising to me.

@DimitrisPapail: "ECHO: Terminal Agents Learn World Models for Free" discusses how CLI agents can predict terminal responses during reinforcement learning, alongside the usual GRPO loss on actions.

